  "audio": "public/audio/brick-holes.wav",
  "duration": 23.006,
  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "A brick has holes punched straight through",
      "start": 0.088,
      "end": 1.786
    },
    {
      "text": "the middle,",
      "start": 1.821,
      "end": 2.308
    },
    {
      "text": "which is an odd thing to do to an",
      "start": 2.404,
      "end": 3.655
    },
    {
      "text": "object whose whole job is being solid.",
      "start": 3.745,
      "end": 5.299
    },
    {
      "text": "The holes make it better.",
      "start": 5.55,
      "end": 6.532
    },
    {
      "text": "Mortar squeezes down into them and sets there,",
      "start": 6.834,
      "end": 8.818
    },
    {
      "text": "so each brick is keyed into the one above",
      "start": 9.086,
      "end": 10.677
    },
    {
      "text": "rather than glued along a flat face.",
      "start": 10.935,
      "end": 12.544
    },
    {
      "text": "Wet clay also has to dry and fire",
      "start": 12.878,
      "end": 14.842
    },
    {
      "text": "without cracking,",
      "start": 15.053,
      "end": 15.713
    },
    {
      "text": "and heat reaches the middle of a perforated",
      "start": 15.947,
      "end": 17.697
    },
    {
      "text": "brick far faster than a solid lump.",
      "start": 17.769,
      "end": 19.395
    },
    {
      "text": "Less clay, less fuel,",
      "start": 19.715,
      "end": 20.912
    },
    {
      "text": "lighter to lift,",
      "start": 21.216,
      "end": 21.77
    },
    {
      "text": "stronger wall.",
      "start": 22.109,
      "end": 22.789
    }
  ],
